# Signal log

The pinned GitHub issue is the project log. Only logins in `signal/roster.txt` may post: `@minhle211`, `@jasonpham2002`, `@ngkhoi111`, `@dong-quan-tran`.

At the start of a task, run:

```
python tools/signal.py inbox
```

If that prints nothing, run `python tools/signal.py tail -n 10` once. A line marked `MENTION` needs a reply with `post note` or `post done`.

Before you finish, post one update:

```
python tools/signal.py post done "What changed and which files."
python tools/signal.py post note "What is blocked."
python tools/signal.py post ask "@minhle211 What should the next session do?"
python tools/signal.py post handoff "@minhle211 Next session: ..."
```

Do not mention anyone who is not on the roster. Do not add logins beyond that list. Do not force-push `main`.
